{"name":"Infinity Pool","hex":"#94d4e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"infinity pool","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of infinity-edge pool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infinity_pool"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infinity pool","blocks":[{"text":"An infinity pool is a reflecting pool or swimming pool where the water flows over one or more edges, producing a visual effect of water with no boundary. Such pools are often designed so that the edge appears to merge with a larger body of water such as the ocean, or with the sky, and may overlook locations such as natural landscapes and cityscapes. They are often seen at hotels, resorts, estates, and in other luxurious places."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_deckchair%29.jpg/330px-SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_deckchair%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infinity_pool"},{"title":"When Saints Go Machine","blocks":[{"text":"When Saints Go Machine is a Danish electropop band from Copenhagen. The group consists of three members: Silas Moldenhawer (drums), Jonas Kenton and Nikolaj Manuel Vonsild (vocals). Until February 2019, there was a fourth member, Simon Muschinsky (keys). Moldenhawer and Kenton are also known from their parallel project, Kenton Slash Demon. When Saints Go Machine brings a more soulful sound than Kenton Slash Demon's rhythmic electro-house music. When Saints Go Machine was formed in 2007 and debuted with their self-titled EP in 2008. In May 2009, they released their debut album Ten Makes a Face. Their most popular songs are \"Fail Forever\", \"You or the Gang\" and \"Kids on Vacation\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/When_Saints_Go_Machine.jpg/330px-When_Saints_Go_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/When_Saints_Go_Machine"},{"title":"Infinity Pool (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Infinity Pool is a 2023 science fiction horror film written and directed by Brandon Cronenberg. The film stars Alexander Skarsgård, Mia Goth, and Cleopatra Coleman. Set in the fictional country of Li Tolqa, it follows struggling novelist James Foster (Skarsgård) and his wife Em (Coleman), a couple on vacation at a seaside resort who, after meeting another couple and having dinner with them, discover the country's dark culture."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Infinity_Pool_poster2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infinity_Pool_(film)"},{"title":"Infinity","blocks":[{"text":"Infinity is something which is boundless, limitless, or endless. It is denoted by ∞, called the infinity symbol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/SierpinskiTriangle.svg/330px-SierpinskiTriangle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infinity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_pool_near_the_edge%29.jpg/500px-SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_pool_near_the_edge%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_pool_near_the_edge%29.jpg/1280px-SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_pool_near_the_edge%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_pool_near_the_edge%29.jpg/500px-SkyPark_Infinity_Pool_%28view_from_pool_near_the_edge%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkyPark_Infinity_Pool_(view_from_pool_near_the_edge).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rosewood_Hong_Kong_Level_6_Swimming_Pool_2020.jpg/500px-Rosewood_Hong_Kong_Level_6_Swimming_Pool_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rosewood_Hong_Kong_Level_6_Swimming_Pool_2020.jpg/1280px-Rosewood_Hong_Kong_Level_6_Swimming_Pool_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rosewood_Hong_Kong_Level_6_Swimming_Pool_2020.jpg/500px-Rosewood_Hong_Kong_Level_6_Swimming_Pool_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The infinity pool with panoramic views of Victoria Harbour at the Rosewood Hong Kong","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosewood_Hong_Kong_Level_6_Swimming_Pool_2020.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Infinity_Edge_Pool%2C_Mauritius.JPG/250px-Infinity_Edge_Pool%2C_Mauritius.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Infinity_Edge_Pool%2C_Mauritius.JPG/330px-Infinity_Edge_Pool%2C_Mauritius.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Infinity_Edge_Pool%2C_Mauritius.JPG/250px-Infinity_Edge_Pool%2C_Mauritius.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInfinity_Edge_Pool%2C_Mauritius.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Movenpick_Maldives_2019.jpg/250px-Movenpick_Maldives_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Movenpick_Maldives_20